.TH AVR\-RUN\-WATCH 1 "" "avr 0.1.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-run-watch \- Watch a workflow run until it completes.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr run watch
[OPTIONS] [RUN_ID]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Watch a workflow run until it completes.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Without RUN_ID, auto-selects the latest in-progress run. Pass --repo
(repeatable) to scope the auto-select to specific repositories.
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr run watch
    avr run watch --repo acme/web
    avr run watch --repo a/x --repo b/y
    avr run watch run-abc123 --exit-status
    avr run watch run-abc123 --ndjson | jq -c .
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
[\fIRUN_ID\fR]
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Scope the auto-select to a repo (org/name or rep-xxx, repeatable). Auto-detected from git remote if omitted. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-exit\-status\fR
Exit non-zero if run failed.
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fIINTEGER\fR
Refresh interval in seconds. (default: 3)
.TP
\fB\-\-ndjson\fR
Force NDJSON event stream (default when stdout isn't a TTY).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-run (1),
.BR avr-run-cancel (1),
.BR avr-run-list (1),
.BR avr-run-logs (1),
.BR avr-run-rerun (1),
.BR avr-run-view (1)
